{"metadata":{"citation_count_without_self_citations":118,"citation_count":142,"publication_info":[{"year":2010,"artid":"205001","journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav.","journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214779"},"journal_volume":"27"}],"core":true,"dois":[{"value":"10.1088/0264-9381/27/20/205001"}],"titles":[{"title":"Next to leading order spin-orbit effects in the motion of inspiralling compact binaries"},{"title":"Next to leading order spin-orbit effects in the motion of inspiralling compact binaries","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"0ae45832-f8c4-45a5-b233-81f8caffd4cf","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/992929"},"full_name":"Porto, Rafael A.","affiliations":[{"value":"Santa Barbara, KITP","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903889"}}],"signature_block":"PARTr","curated_relation":true}],"curated":true,"figures":[{"key":"8c102248865e2e593d6417be7f455e8b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/8c102248865e2e593d6417be7f455e8b","source":"arxiv","caption":"\\sl One-graviton contributions linear in spin at ${\\cal O}(v^5)$. A dashed line represents a potential graviton, a blob account for spin insertions at each PN order from Eqs. (\\ref{sgnr1}--\\ref{sgnr2}), and a black dot stands for `propagator' corrections as explained in the text.","filename":"onegSO2.png"},{"key":"d34b4ea16cea3f3aae4d6264f0ceb3ea","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/d34b4ea16cea3f3aae4d6264f0ceb3ea","source":"arxiv","caption":"\\sl Non-linear gravitational effects due the couplings in Eqs. (\\ref{sgh2v4}, \\ref{sgh2v5}) and (\\ref{h2m}, \\ref{h2mv}).","filename":"segSO2.png"},{"key":"16c5bdc788932b2aa9f4ca81ca559e9e","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/16c5bdc788932b2aa9f4ca81ca559e9e","source":"arxiv","caption":"\\sl Non-linear gravitational effects due to the three-graviton couplings. A black dot represents an extra power of $v$ from a time derivative in the three graviton vertex (see text.)","filename":"benzSO2.png"},{"key":"1285d3281b5597ca1881e581f34836df","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/1285d3281b5597ca1881e581f34836df","source":"arxiv","caption":"\\sl Type of divergences in the three-graviton diagrams","filename":"div2.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["Porto:2010tr"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"binary: compact","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"higher-order: 1","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"gravitation: potential","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"effective field theory","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"spin","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"graviton","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"Feynman graph","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"Using effective field theory (EFT) techniques we calculate the next-to-leading order (NLO) spin-orbit contributions to the gravitational potential of inspiralling compact binaries. We use the covariant spin supplementarity condition (SSC), and explicitly prove the equivalence with previous results by Faye et al. in arXiv:gr-qc/0605139. We also show that the direct application of the Newton-Wigner SSC at the level of the action leads to the correct dynamics using a canonical (Dirac) algebra. This paper then completes the calculation of the necessary spin dynamics within the EFT formalism that will be used in a separate paper to compute the spin contributions to the energy flux and phase evolution to NLO.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/348147"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"325","page_start":"325","journal_title":"Science","journal_volume":"256"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/272672"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"518","page_start":"518","journal_title":"Nucl.Instrum.Meth.A","journal_volume":"289"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.n